    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d122">

                <pb facs="0332" n="293" xml:id="pg293"/>

                <head>122. Memorandum From the Executive Secretary of the 40 Committee (Ratliff) to
                    Director of Central Intelligence Colby<anchor n="1" xml:id="d122-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1975-07-28">July 28, 1975</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Angola</item>
                </list>
                <p>On 27 July 1975 higher authority approved the full [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >dollar amount not declassified</hi>] program incorporated in the NSC task
                    group paper “Plan for Covert Action—Angola” which was submitted 16 July
                        1975.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d122-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>This includes the previous approval noted in the minute of 21 July 1975,<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d122-f3"/> adding [<hi rendition="#italic">dollar amount not
                        declassified</hi>] of Phase II of the plan for a total approval of [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">dollar amount not declassified</hi>]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Rob Roy Ratliff</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
